# BBSFirewall - Status endpoint IP allowlist
#
# Source IPs / CIDRs allowed to call GET /status (the unauthenticated uptime-
# monitor endpoint on the config editor's HTTPS port, e.g. for Uptime Kuma).
# There is no API key or login on this endpoint — this file is the ONLY gate.
#
# One IP or CIDR per line. IPv4 and IPv6 both work. Lines starting with # are
# comments; an inline # comment after an entry is also allowed.
#
# IMPORTANT: unlike api-trustedhosts.txt, an EMPTY or MISSING file here DOES
# lock everyone out — same fail-closed behavior as trustedhosts.txt. There is
# no key to fall back on, so add your monitoring host's IP before relying on
# this endpoint.
#
# Examples:
#   203.0.113.10           the Uptime Kuma server
#   198.51.100.0/24        a hosting range
#   2001:db8:abcd::/48     an IPv6 range
#
# To use this file:
# 1. Copy to status-trustedhosts.txt
# 2. Add the IP(s) your uptime monitor polls from
# 3. Set STATUS_TRUSTEDHOSTS_PATH=./status-trustedhosts.txt in your .env (this is the default)

# 203.0.113.10
# 198.51.100.0/24
